{"w": 595.3200073242188, "h": 809.0257568359375, "lines": [{"t": "57", "x": 0.9038164196379167, "y": 0.9742087522985531, "w": 0.02992682896571904, "h": 0.017428414981790374, "c": 1, "size": 12.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "READING PASSAGE 3", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.1635769891357863, "w": 0.29152886031313374, "h": 0.023179739115831682, "c": 1, "size": 16.0, "bold": true}, {"t": "You should spend about 20 minutes on Question 27- 40, which are based on", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.2082529616196902, "w": 0.8272887440006241, "h": 0.02039118517446672, "c": 1, "size": 14.0, "bold": true}, {"t": "Reading Passage 3 below", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.2386598743515504, "w": 0.277090834956047, "h": 0.02039118517446672, "c": 1, "size": 14.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "Invasion of the Robot Umpires", "x": 0.301837667524493, "y": 0.2791381914161501, "w": 0.4390881820203424, "h": 0.026142565890596797, "c": 1, "size": 18.0, "bold": true}, {"t": "A few years ago, Fred DeJesus from Brooklyn, New York became the first umpire", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.3283677395183944, "w": 0.8266385307435941, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "in a minor league baseball game to use something called the Automated Ball-", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.35654976907717933, "w": 0.8215326855191603, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "Strike System (ABS), often referred to as the 'robe-umpire'. Instead of making any", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.384880194594102, "w": 0.8266195636271401, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "judgments himself about a strike*, DeJesus had decisions fed to him through an", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.4132105446682396, "w": 0.8268327130061003, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "earpiece, connected to a modified missile-tracking system. The contraption", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.44154089474237723, "w": 0.8264776690910742, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "looked like a large black pizza box with one glowing green eye; it was mounted", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.469895990050002, "w": 0.8259467948802729, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "above the press stand.", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.4982263778455321, "w": 0.233916679815492, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "Major League Baseball (MLB), who had commissioned the system, wanted human", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.536494617383617, "w": 0.826229353652959, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "umpires to announce the calls, just as they would have done in the past. When the", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.5648250051791472, "w": 0.8261932648692197, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "first pitch came in, a recorded voice told DeJesus it was a strike. Previously, calling", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.5931553552532848, "w": 0.8268583442445515, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "a strike was a judgment call on the part of the umpire. Even if the batter does not", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.6695806693857252, "w": 0.8261206772019258, "h": 0.018822673091776602, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "hit the ball, a pitch that passes through the 'strike zone' (an imaginary zone about", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.6979109440170779, "w": 0.8263836537084353, "h": 0.018822673091776602, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "seventeen inches wide, stretching from the batter's knees to the middle of his", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.7262413695340004, "w": 0.8260336335161456, "h": 0.018822673091776602, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "chest) is considered a strike. During that first game, when DeJesus announced", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.7545717196081381, "w": 0.825837503279517, "h": 0.018822673091776602, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "calls, there was no heckling and no shouted disagreement. Nobody said a word.", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.7829020696822757, "w": 0.8087167587186964, "h": 0.018822673091776602, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "For a hundred and fifty years or so, the strike zone has been the game's animating", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.8210220264264005, "w": 0.8262511914681194, "h": 0.018822673091776602, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "force-countless arguments between a team's manager and the umpire have taken", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.8493523765005382, "w": 0.826192034569774, "h": 0.018822673091776602, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "place over its boundaries and whether a ball had crossed through it. The rules of", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.8777074718081629, "w": 0.8263158847139702, "h": 0.018822673091776602, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "play have evolved in various stages. Today, everyone knows that you may scream", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.9060378973250856, "w": 0.8260772066215126, "h": 0.018822673091776602, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "your disagreement in an umpire's face, but you must never shout personal abuse", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.9343682473992232, "w": 0.8260553688063522, "h": 0.018822673091776602, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}], "source": "pdf text layer"}